  "mathematical_scope": [
    "The actual uniform divided-factor upper tower and raw-optical-derived reciprocal bound are evaluated at the same physical root, current state, and root factor g.",
    "The low order is max(factorLow,max(powerLow,factorLoss)); the last term controls the factor zero value without absorbing a high-order seminorm into a low constant.",
    "Only a fixed scaling C0 of the same T.E0 is used to achieve W>=1. E0 itself is not assumed >=1; reciprocal coefficient and exponent are both explicitly dominated by K0.",
    "The existing positive-power polynomial theorem supplies all ordinary derivatives, including zero, for every real power gamma, with common low order and loss chosen before gamma.",
    "All constants precede state, component, host, side, factor g, strip radius, point and derivative order; no chosen-radius inverse appears."
  ],
